WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.835
-My next guest has been selected
to five NFL pro bowls

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:06.205
and is one of the greatest tight
ends to ever play the game.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:09.242
On Sunday, he won his fourth
Super Bowl ring

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.344
and his first as a member
of the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:15.315
Here is one of our favorites,
Rob Gronkowski.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.782
Gronk!

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:19.252
-What's up, Jimmy? I got
to give a cheers to that, baby.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.920
-Come on.
-Super Bowl champs.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.356
-I got to say, buddy,
I was so happy for you.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.125
Congratulations, first of all.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.194 line:0%
I was happy just from
the first touchdown.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.362 line:0%
When you caught that,
I go, "That's it.

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:32.232 line:0%
That's all I need.
That's the win right there.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.499 line:0%
Just take that."

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:35.535 line:0%
And I'm just so psyched,
'cause you know we love you.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.971
And you're just fun
every single time.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.741
And you're so -- I just --
Everybody loves you.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.876
Everyone's rooting for you, pal.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.245
And then you announced
your retirement,

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.716
and I go, "Yeah,
I guess I'm down with that."

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.450
I just want you to play forever.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.752
But I'm like,
"Okay, I understand.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.320
He's smart.
He wants to get out."

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.055
Then you end up on
"Masked Singer."

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:58.458
You're the white tiger
on "Masked Singer."

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.628
Gosh, what a weird year.
It is so fascinating.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.863
You went from White Tiger
to winning the Super Bowl.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:05.031
How does it feel --

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.532
I know you're doing
a bunch of interviews.

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.800
Has it sunk in yet?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.736
You're a four-time
Super Bowl champion, bud.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.205
-Yes, you know, it really
hasn't sunken in yet.

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:15.241
Yeah, I've been just talking
to my friends and family,

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.810
I'm like, it feels like surreal.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.545
Like, it feels like, you know,
like it didn't even happen.

00:01:19.545 --> 00:01:20.846
But it did happen.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.915
Like, it just happened
with like a blink of an eye.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:27.420
I just remember being traded to
Tampa Bay like it was yesterday.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.188
And then a whole season
has happened,

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.056
with the whole pandemic going on
and everything.

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:33.059
It's just been an amazing ride.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.727
It's been an amazing journey.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.995
And it's actually
just incredible.

00:01:36.995 --> 00:01:39.832
Like you said, I was the white
tiger on "Masked Singer."

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.767
You know?
And I was talking football

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:45.738
on Fox for a couple weeks,
end of the last season.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.340
And then I had
a Super Bowl party

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.708
last year at the Super Bowl,

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.376
and then I come back
out of retirement,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.444
and then, you're right.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.145
I'm like, "Whoa,
we're in the playoffs."

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:55.882
Like, this is an incredible
year. Back to the playoffs.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:59.051
You know, the Bucs haven't been
to the playoffs since 2007.

00:01:59.051 --> 00:02:04.056
And then all of a sudden, win
three away games on the road.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:06.258
Washington,
they had a top-10 defense.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.861
New Orleans, they beat us twice
in regular season,

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.195
with Drew Brees.

00:02:10.195 --> 00:02:12.432
We go there, they have a top-10
defense, beat them,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:16.336
and then go to Green Bay, you
know, with that tradition there,

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:19.305
and just win
versus the MVP, Aaron Rodgers.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.740
It's just an incredible journey.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.675
And then go to the Super Bowl
at our home stadium,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.844
first time ever,
and win it all, man.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.212
It's been an incredible ride.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.946
And it's been surreal, man.

00:02:27.946 --> 00:02:30.349
-You caught two
touchdown passes,

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.484
and of course, you had
to do the Gronk spike,

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:36.189
which is awesome and hopefully
trademarked and whatever.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:39.225
And, dude, that should be an
alcoholic beverage,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.693
the Gronk Spike.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.094
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.897
Dang, that's true.
-You just put a little spike

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.665
in your juice,
in your orange juice.

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.767
-That could be dangerous.
-But it's Gronk Spike.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.235
It could be dangerous.
-I know.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.602
-It could be fun.
-Yeah.

00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:52.338
-Dude, start talking to people.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.440
You know who to talk to.
-It could be deadly.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.474
I love it.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:56.643
But, dude, look at the spike.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:58.811
Please show this thing,
because I love it.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.214 line:0%
It's just extreme!

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.083 line:0%
And you go for it.
-Oh.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.918
-If I did that,
and I really practiced,

00:03:05.918 --> 00:03:07.786
and I spent like
probably, you know,

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.755
10 years of my life
focusing on that,

00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:11.857
here's what would happen
with me. I would spike it,

00:03:11.857 --> 00:03:13.960
and it would probably bounce
and hit me in the helmet.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.761
And it would be
all over the Internet.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:18.931
Is there a way to throw it

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:21.734
so that it doesn't
go back in your face?

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.836
-Well, I got two bloopers
in my life before.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.438
But the way to throw is you just
put your palm on the football,

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:29.842
and then, you know, with a good,
great grip using your palm.

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.011
And then when you bounce it,
you kind of bounce it

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.746
with the belly of the football,
you know,

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.348
the big part of the football
where it sticks out.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:38.084
And then it hits the ground
high, with full potential.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:41.554
And then that gives it its best
chance to bounce the highest

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.988
is when it hits off the belly.

00:03:42.988 --> 00:03:46.993
But I've had it before
where it has came back at me

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.894
and hit me
right in the you-know-where.

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:50.095
You know, the gonads.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.530
And I was like, "Ooh."

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.132
-Wait, I don't know
what you mean.

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.968
What do you mean by gonads?

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.502
Let me google gonads. Siri.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:59.572
-Yeah, gonads, it's, you know,
a little slang for --

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.174
-Siri.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.476
Siri. What are g--

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.144
Siri. What are --

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.646
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.514
I don't know
what I'm talking about.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.916
-Yeah, I don't know
if Siri knows --

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.218
If Siri knows what gonads are,
I mean --

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.486
-This is nothing but perfect.

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:15.554
The photos, every photo of you,
you look great.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:17.289
You and Tom, there's a picture

00:04:17.289 --> 00:04:19.658
of you guys taking in
the Super Bowl win together.

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:21.393
How does that relationship work

00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.362
between you and the quarterback,
you and Tom?

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:26.432
Do you guys -- When you first
started and you met him,

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.335
did you have to like go hang out
with him after practice?

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:32.038
Did you go see movies?
What'd you do?

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.939
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.442
It's a great question.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.277
You know, as a rookie,
it's a little,

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:39.745
you know, it's a little
difficult task.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:42.581
I mean, it's kind of hard
to, you know, get yourself in

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.917
and build up that chemistry
with the quarterback.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:48.021
But when I was a rookie,
actually, Tom --

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.188
When I got into the league,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.857
Tom was actually still older
than I am now.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:54.393
He was 32 years old
when I started playing.

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:57.229
And I'm only 31 right now.
So that's pretty incredible.

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.431
Like, I retired,
came back, came to Tampa,

00:04:59.431 --> 00:05:02.501
and I'm still not even his age
when I first met him,

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.735
which is incredible.

00:05:03.735 --> 00:05:05.070
-That's bizarre.
-But like --

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.639
Yeah, obviously,
when I first met him,

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.040
like I was like, "Ooh,"
you know, like --

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.242
You know, it's Tom.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.176
Like, it just
this dream come true.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:13.712
And then I just saw
the way that everyone worked.

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:15.047
And when I came in as a rookie,

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:17.349
I was open-minded
just to get it done,

00:05:17.349 --> 00:05:21.187
whatever I had to do, you know,
to be respected,

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.389
to get out on the field,
to get some playing time.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.924
And let me tell you,
he works you.

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.225
He grinds you sometimes.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:30.096
Like, he can get you, too,
like, man, like --

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.730
-Right?
-He wants me to keep going?

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.900
He wants me to keep going?
I already did 50 routes.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.301
Like, oh, 10 more?

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.770
Like, and he won't take a no.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.607
-Your first three Super Bowls
came with the Patriots.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:44.777
Have you talked
to Belichick at all?

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:45.978
-No, I have not.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:47.379
-You haven't received
any voicemails

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:50.383
of somebody going like [Growls]

00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:51.917
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:53.352
No, no, I have not.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.721
-[ Chuckles ]
You have to call that guy.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.723
Come on. You got to get him
on speakerphone right now

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.792
and be like, "Yo!"
-You give him a call.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.159
He was on your show before.
-I'm afraid of him!

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:02.895
I'm afraid of him.
I'm not going to call that dude.

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.529
Are you kidding me, man?

00:06:04.529 --> 00:06:05.998
Hey, we love you, man.

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.601
Keep it up and just, I don't
know, keep being awesome.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:11.237
I'm sure we're gonna see you
back next season.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.839
You have to.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.339
-Yeah. Yeah, hopefully, man.

00:06:14.339 --> 00:06:17.310
I don't see why I won't be
back with the Bucs.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.146
But we can have a great team
coming back, too.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.180
Obviously, we just won it all.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.217
Super Bowl LV champs.

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.851
Tampa Bay Buccaneers, baby.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:28.820
But, you know, it's already two
days, you know, past the game,

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:29.922
and I'm already thinking, like,

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.191
"Man, what's it going to be like
next year?

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.926
Can we make it back?
What do I got to do?"

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.561
So, that's already in my mind.

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:36.829
Pretty crazy.

00:06:36.829 --> 00:06:39.232
-Keep us guessing.
Keep us guessing.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.632
I don't know
what you're going to do next.

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:43.068
-Maybe I'll retire again.

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:45.471
Hey, I got an idea.
I got an idea.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.640
Maybe I'll retire just so
I don't do training camp,

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.041
'cause training camp, like --

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.177
-That's the worst part.
-Yeah.

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.078
-Brilliant.
-Training camp, like --

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.246
Yeah. And then I'll come back

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:56.081
like oh, oh,
a week before the --

00:06:56.081 --> 00:07:00.653
"Hey, will you guys
take me back?

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:02.321
Okay, yeah, yeah,
I'll come back. Yeah.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:04.056
Oh, it's game time?
Oh, perfect."

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.958
-Congratulations.
Enjoy it. Enjoy it.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.226
You worked hard. Enjoy it.

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.661
Thank you so much
for doing our show.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:10.896
I appreciate it, buddy.
-No problem, man.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.866
-Four-time Super Bowl champion
Rob Gronkowski, everybody.

